WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.250
Two doors.

2
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:05.840
Behind the first, a ten-year-old
girl is locked in a red bedroom.

3
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:08.310
A faint light glides up the wall.

4
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:13.030
In a tall mirror, a "strange
little figure" stares back at her.

5
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:17.790
Years later, another house: a
dim corridor of black doors.

6
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.580
Behind the last, someone laughs.

7
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.020
One locked room could just be a scare.

8
00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.250
So why does the novel give us two?

9
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.240
In this mission, you'll
learn the Gothic toolkit:

10
00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:32.800
old mansions, locked rooms,
secrets and the supernatural.

11
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.620
You'll see how Brontë
often explains it away.

12
00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:36.480
That light?

13
00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.940
Perhaps "a gleam from a lantern".

14
00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:42.610
And you'll step inside it
yourself, and face that mirror.

15
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.690
Your mission: work out why the
novel has two locked rooms.
